(a) change `ordered[5].binder` from `"(q,t0)"` to `"q"` and add a separate... no, that breaks the tuple semantics.
(b) edit `formal` to write `not exists (q,t0) in D5 with ...` — i.e., make the formal sentence use the declared tuple binder.
(c) loosen R03 to accept a binder if all its components appear in `formal`.

